    "test_goal": "Check repeated submission of one pending project creation and distinguish it from two deliberate completed creations.\nRequired checks: [{\"goal_id\": \"repeat-create\", \"description\": \"As member2, submit project_name twice while the first creation is still pending. Capture evidence that both requests belong to the same pending operation, then inspect the settled project rows and refresh. Separately create intentional_project_name twice only after each previous operation has finished; these are distinct operations.\", \"feature\": \"Project\", \"identity_reference\": \"member2\", \"expected_behavior_ids\": [\"EB-PROJECT-SUBMIT\"], \"test_data_keys\": [\"member2_username\", \"project_name\", \"intentional_project_name\"], \"independent_group\": \"workflow\"}]\nCompletion requirements: [\"For ordinary navigation, wait for the selected view and its project data to finish loading before issuing another view navigation or project selection in the same context. Pending-create submission tests intentionally repeat the pending submit operation. Independent contexts may run concurrently.\", \"Cover every required test goal with executable, scoped checks and explicit identity assignments. Preserve meaningful independent goal groups and required live-session ordering.\", \"Record actual goal assertions and observed results, including rejected operations, persistence, and immediate display checks. Finding a reproducible deviation still completes a testing goal.\", \"For each reported deviation record expected versus actual behavior, acting identity, project/task reference, ordered actions, and timestamped browser evidence. Use two matching fresh reproduction attempts within three attempts plus independent fresh verification; keep unresolved results uncertain.\", \"The final summary must faithfully describe completed, failed, and uncertain checks, finding statuses, evidence, and recorded metrics. Do not infer success from task completion text.\"]",
